48	/**
49	 * Recognises Lobu's first-party surfaces (CLI, Mac/iOS bridges) so the UI can
50	 * fold them into a "your devices & tools" group instead of listing them
51	 * alongside third-party MCP apps. Prefers the exact software-id allowlist;
52	 * the "Lobu …" client-name check is a best-effort fallback for clients that
53	 * register without a known software id (and could in theory be spoofed — this
54	 * is a display category, not an access boundary).
